# AccentAI – Project Rules

## What This App Is
AccentAI is an iOS mobile app built with Expo Router and TypeScript.
It is an accent training app that helps users improve their spoken
English by reading passages aloud and receiving real-time AI scoring.
The target user is a native English speaker wanting to refine their
accent toward British RP or American General American.

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Expo (Expo Router for navigation)
- Language: TypeScript (.tsx files)
- Platform: iOS first (React Native)
- Font: Outfit (via @expo-google-fonts/outfit)
- Icons: @expo/vector-icons (Ionicons, stroke style only)
- Navigation: Expo Router tab-based navigation, 4 tabs

## File Structure
app/
  _layout.tsx        → root layout, tab navigator
  (tabs)/
    index.tsx        → Home screen
    practice.tsx     → Practice screen
    progress.tsx     → Progress screen
    settings.tsx     → Settings screen
constants/
  colours.ts         → ALL colour tokens, dark + light mode
  typography.ts      → font sizes, weights, line heights
  spacing.ts         → spacing scale
components/
  Ringstat.tsx       → reusable accuracy ring component
  SessionRow.tsx     → reusable recent session row
  StatCard.tsx       → reusable dark stat card

## Design System — NEVER deviate from this

### Light Mode (Indigo)
- Page background:    #eef0f8
- Card background:    #ffffff
- Card border:        #d0d4e8
- Section background: #eef0f8
- Primary text:       #181c30
- Muted text:         #9098b0
- Divider:            #eaecf4
- Accent:             #4f62d0 (indigo blue)
- Accent secondary:   #6ee7f7 (cyan — trend/highlight only)
- CTA button bg:      #4f62d0
- CTA button text:    #ffffff
- Stat card bg:       #181c30 (dark card on light bg — intentional)
- Stat card text:     #e0e4f8
- Stat card muted:    #4a5080
- Stat card ring:     #4f62d0
- Stat card border:   #2a3060
- Toggle on:          #4f62d0
- Toggle off:         #e0e4ee
- Nav active:         #4f62d0
- Nav inactive:       #b0b8d0
- Score good (75%+):  #e8ebf8 bg / #4f62d0 text
- Score avg (50-74%): #fef9e8 bg / #c09010 text
- Score poor (<50%):  #fde8e8 bg / #c03030 text

### Dark Mode (Indigo Dark)
- Page background:    #0e1020
- Card background:    #141830
- Card border:        #1e2448
- Primary text:       #c8d0f0
- Muted text:         #3a4060
- Divider:            #1a2040
- Accent:             #6680f0 (brighter indigo for dark bg)
- Accent secondary:   #50d8f0 (cyan — trend/highlight only)
- CTA button bg:      #6680f0
- CTA button text:    #ffffff
- Stat ring:          #6680f0
- Stat ring track:    #1a2040
- Toggle on:          #6680f0
- Nav active:         #6680f0
- Nav inactive:       #2a3460
- Score good (75%+):  #1a2252 bg / #6680f0 text
- Score avg (50-74%): #2a2010 bg / #d0a030 text
- Score poor (<50%):  #2a1010 bg / #d05050 text

### Typography (Outfit font throughout)
- Wordmark:           13px weight 700 tracking -0.3px
- Screen title:       20px weight 700 tracking -0.6px
- Section label:      9px weight 700 tracking 1.3px UPPERCASE
- Card title:         15-16px weight 700 tracking -0.4px
- Body:               12-13px weight 400 line-height 1.7
- Meta/caption:       10px weight 400
- Stat number large:  40-48px weight 700-800 tracking -2.5px
- Stat number small:  16-17px weight 700
- Ring number:        13-15px weight 700

### Spacing
- Horizontal page padding:  14px
- Card padding:             14-16px
- Card border radius:       20px
- Small card border radius: 14-16px
- Button border radius:     11-12px
- Badge border radius:      8-10px
- Gap between cards:        12px
- Section gap:              18-20px

### Key Component Patterns

#### RingStat (accuracy ring)
- Always dark card (#141830 dark / #181c30 light) regardless of mode
- 70x70px ring, 6px track, 6px fill
- Track colour: #1a2040 (dark) / #2a3060 (light)
- Fill colour: accent
- Centre text: percentage, weight 700, 14-15px, white
- Below ring: label row with dividers between streak / words / trend
- Trend always uses cyan accent (#50d8f0 dark / #6ee7f7 light)

#### SessionRow
- No card wrapper — flat rows with bottom divider
- 38x38px score badge, border-radius 10px
- Badge colour from score bracket (good/avg/poor tokens above)
- Session name: 12px weight 600
- Meta line: 10px muted

#### NavBar
- 4 tabs: Home (house), Practice (mic), Progress (bar chart), Settings (cog)
- Ionicons stroke style only — NEVER filled icons
- Active tab: accent colour icon + accent label weight 600
- Inactive tab: nav inactive colour
- Always sticky bottom, always has top border divider

#### GB/US Toggle
- Vertical pill, rounded 10-12px
- Active: accent bg, white text weight 700
- Inactive: transparent, muted text
- Always top-right of screen header or inside hero card

#### Toggle Switch (settings)
- 38x22px pill
- On: accent colour bg, white thumb right
- Off: muted bg, white thumb left
- Thumb: 18x18px white circle with subtle shadow

#### Progress Bars (word scores)
- 60px wide, 4px height, border-radius 3px
- Track: divider colour
- Fill: accent (good), amber (avg), red (poor)
- Score label right-aligned, 10px weight 700

## Colour Mode Rules
- ALWAYS use useColorScheme() from react-native
- ALWAYS import ALL colours from constants/colours.ts
- NEVER hardcode any hex value inside a component file
- Usage pattern: const t = scheme === 'dark' ? tokens.dark : tokens.light
- The RingStat card is ALWAYS dark regardless of mode — this is intentional

## Code Rules
- NEVER hardcode hex colours in component files
- NEVER use emoji as icons
- NEVER use filled Ionicons — stroke only
- ALWAYS use StyleSheet.create() — never inline style objects
- ALWAYS use SafeAreaView as root container
- ALWAYS use ScrollView on screens where content may overflow
- ALWAYS use TypeScript — no .js files, no 'any' types
- Keep each screen file under 300 lines — extract to /components if needed
- Shared components go in /components with their own Props type

## Screen-by-Screen Spec

### Home (index.tsx)
- Sticky status bar + sticky bottom nav
- Greeting: date muted above, large bold name greeting left, GB/US toggle top-right
- RingStat card: accuracy ring + streak / words / trend stats
- Up Next card: white card, session name, meta, 7-bar week progress, CTA button
- Weekly bar chart: 7 bars M-S, filled vs unfilled
- Recent Sessions: flat list of SessionRows, 4 visible before scroll

### Practice (practice.tsx)
- Header: passage name muted above, "Speak aloud" title, GB/US toggle
- Passage card: white card, highlighted key words in accent tint
- Live Score card: always dark, RingStat ring + pronunciation/rhythm progress bars
- Audio waveform: white card, bar visualiser
- Record button: large circle button centred, mic icon, accent bg
- Below button: status label ("Recording… tap to stop" / "Tap to start")

### Progress (progress.tsx)
- Header: "Your journey" muted above, "Progress" title
- Accuracy trend card: dark card, SVG line chart, 7d/30d toggle pills top-right
- Streak calendar card: dark card, 7-column grid, today highlighted with cyan border
- Best words card: dark card, top 2-3 words with indigo fill bars + percentages
- Needs work card: dark card, bottom 2-3 words with red/amber fill bars

### Settings (settings.tsx)
- Avatar header: indigo circle with initials, name bold, streak + accuracy subtitle
- Profile section: white card, Name row (chevron), Default accent toggle
- Appearance section: white card, Dark mode toggle switch
- Notifications section: white card, Daily reminder row + time, Streak alerts toggle
- About section: white card, Version row, Privacy policy row (chevron)


## App Data Model (current, will expand)
User:
  - name: string
  - streak: number
  - totalWords: number
  - accuracy: number (0-100)
  - accentMode: 'GB' | 'US'

Session:
  - id: string
  - name: string        e.g. "Reading Passage 3"
  - meta: string        e.g. "14 words · British · Today"
  - score: number       0-100
  - result: 'good' | 'avg' | 'poor'
  - date: string

Passage:
  - id: string
  - title: string
  - body: string
  - wordCount: number
  - accentMode: 'GB' | 'US'
  - highlightedWords: string[]   key words to highlight in the passage card

LiveScore:
  - overall: number
  - pronunciation: number
  - rhythm: number
  - isRecording: boolean

## What to Always Do Before Writing Code
1. Read ALL rules above
2. Import colours from constants/colours.ts only
3. Check which screen/component you are editing
4. Match the design system exactly — no improvising
5. If anything is unclear, ask before assuming